   "topic": "verb-type-3",
   "heading": "Verb type 3",
   "text": "The infinitive (the dictionary form) ends in la/lä or sta/stä (also na/nä, ra/rä). To inflect the verb, remove the final two letters of the infinitive and then add the vowel e and the personal ending. Verbs mennä and panna also belong to this group even though they end in nna/nnä. Some common type 3 verbs: kävellä (to walk), shoppailla (to shop), keskustella (to talk, to discuss).",
